554
00:30:07,421 --> 00:30:12,460
There was one truck bigger than the rest of them, Bigfoot,

555
00:30:12,461 --> 00:30:16,140
owned and souped up by Bob Chandler.

556
00:30:16,141 --> 00:30:19,980
Bigfoot was the largest monster truck of its era.

557
00:30:19,981 --> 00:30:24,380
Bob Chandler was the first guy to design a monster truck

558
00:30:24,381 --> 00:30:27,880
and it was a 1974 Ford F-250.

559
00:30:27,881 --> 00:30:30,720
Everything that he put on it was larger than it should be,

560
00:30:30,721 --> 00:30:33,180
and he would take the truck itself

561
00:30:33,181 --> 00:30:35,060
and run it over other cars,

562
00:30:35,061 --> 00:30:36,920
and every time the truck broke,

563
00:30:36,921 --> 00:30:40,760
he would rebuild it only with bigger and larger parts

564
00:30:40,761 --> 00:30:42,500
every single time.

565
00:30:42,501 --> 00:30:45,140
Event promoters eventually caught wind,

566
00:30:45,141 --> 00:30:47,640
inviting Chandler to put on an event

567
00:30:47,641 --> 00:30:51,500
to showcase what Bigfoot could do.

568
00:30:54,380 --> 00:30:56,880
The first monster truck rally was at,

569
00:30:56,881 --> 00:31:00,880
was in Pontiac, Michigan at the Silverdome in 1982.

570
00:31:00,881 --> 00:31:03,720
Bigfoot was equipped with 66-inch tires

571
00:31:03,721 --> 00:31:08,220
and crushed two vehicles in front of 70,000 people.

572
00:31:08,221 --> 00:31:11,760
And where the series got its actual name,

573
00:31:11,761 --> 00:31:13,760
the monster truck shows.

574
00:31:13,761 --> 00:31:17,340
By the mid-'80s, the U.S. Hot Rod Association

575
00:31:17,341 --> 00:31:20,880
created official head-to-head competitions,

576
00:31:20,881 --> 00:31:27,320
competitions, and to this day, it hosts Monster Truck shows at venues and sold out arenas

577
00:31:27,321 --> 00:31:34,560
